{
    "word": "clayey",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                "word": "clayey",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "85146e42-9b2d-49cd-b1ec-b914491c9c4e",
                        "entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "clayier"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9618db57-88b7-430a-8822-658bb8670f6c",
                        "entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "clayiest"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e1d0f94-77bf-3889-a303-8a4c475a3c51",
                        "entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Composed of clay or containing (much) clay; clayish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ff9b3ab-1aa0-4c38-9389-8a03b8b8aebb",
                                "sense_id": "2e1d0f94-77bf-3889-a303-8a4c475a3c51",
                                "text": "The shores of the rivers and creeks are chiefly planted with coffee, to the distance of about 30 miles from the sea; thence 30 miles farther up, the soil becomes clayey and more fit for sugar[-]canes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30e56b99-f34c-4904-90f2-040d7b3c6654",
                                "sense_id": "2e1d0f94-77bf-3889-a303-8a4c475a3c51",
                                "text": "She had walked over rotted, decaying, splintered planks covered with clayey soil: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "917eb1b8-19e2-4c5a-9be7-8a23126e0872",
                                "sense_id": "2e1d0f94-77bf-3889-a303-8a4c475a3c51",
                                "text": "Limestone, of course, is calcium carbonate, and thus chemically utterly different in composition from the clayey rocks below and the hard, pebbly ones above."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0a8cb9be-f1bc-3324-87d4-249ad88329fd",
                        "entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Covered or dirtied with clay."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abf15060-5b88-4cba-a5a1-b389bb596fba",
                                "sense_id": "0a8cb9be-f1bc-3324-87d4-249ad88329fd",
                                "text": "Wheat-fields, one would think, cannot come to grow untilled; no man made clayey, or made weary thereby;—unless machinery will do it?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "022e6799-f67e-3458-867e-b5fb27ff9079",
                        "entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling clay; claylike, clayish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "82de5875-2569-4caa-9fef-23e22e3a84d2",
                                "sense_id": "022e6799-f67e-3458-867e-b5fb27ff9079",
                                "text": "Death, grim Death, will fold / Me, in his leaden Arms, and preſs me cloſe / To his cold clayie Breaſt: […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1af28081-16b1-3902-9623-9c4a9cb28e7a",
                        "entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of the human body, as contrasted with the soul; bodily, human, mortal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "069832ed-3f22-477b-84da-b601044f9d76",
                                "sense_id": "1af28081-16b1-3902-9623-9c4a9cb28e7a",
                                "text": "This purifing of wit, this enritching of memory, enabling of iudgment, and enlarging of conceyt, which commonly we call learning, […] the final end is, to lead and draw vs to as high a perfection, as our degenerate ſoules made worſe by their clayey lodgings, can be capable of."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd9eaa8b-b139-4257-86e3-8f9c06d4215f",
                                "sense_id": "1af28081-16b1-3902-9623-9c4a9cb28e7a",
                                "text": "[A]mid these tombs, / Cold as their clayey tenants, know, my heart / Must never grow to stone!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2159ecb7-76f1-448a-946a-12493aa2f7f7",
                                "sense_id": "1af28081-16b1-3902-9623-9c4a9cb28e7a",
                                "text": "To low estate of clayey creature, / See, I bring the beggar's meed, / Nutriment beyond the need!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78f08303-028d-436d-8108-362e4c752c77",
                                "sense_id": "1af28081-16b1-3902-9623-9c4a9cb28e7a",
                                "text": "[W]hen between sheets, whether by day or by night, and whether asleep or awake, I have a way of always keeping my eyes shut, in order the more to concentrate the snugness of being in bed. Because no man can ever feel his own identity aright except his eyes be closed; as if, darkness were indeed the proper element of our essences, though light be more congenial to our clayey part."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d50cfb98-e3f0-4856-87cf-638f01b5a35b",
                        "source_entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "source_sense_description": "composed of clay or containing (much) clay",
                        "target_lang_word": "argileux",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "argileux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a62a1884-ebe8-3a98-9d3a-acf4efbd7d1f",
                                        "entry_id": "640953fa-91d7-316f-9c78-91b0c3dfda7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui tient de l’argile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fdd9e16-d355-4584-a109-a9fd822c6857",
                                                "sense_id": "a62a1884-ebe8-3a98-9d3a-acf4efbd7d1f",
                                                "text": "Ce sont des calcaires compactes, sub-lithographiques, dont quelques-uns ont un faux aspect de calcaire grossier marin, et d’autres qui sont celluleux, alternent avec des marnes plus ou moins argileuses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f56cf3b-bc9b-48b7-bf00-87cc754688fb",
                                                "sense_id": "a62a1884-ebe8-3a98-9d3a-acf4efbd7d1f",
                                                "text": "La grande et la moyenne ont des assolements semblables; ils sont triennaux dans les coteaux argilo-calcaires et les plaines argileuses, et biennaux dans les terres d'alluvion et les boulbènes légères."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56613f44-86c1-4d67-8df5-5461e12bc1d2",
                                                "sense_id": "a62a1884-ebe8-3a98-9d3a-acf4efbd7d1f",
                                                "text": "Dans les sols légers et perméables la potasse sera fournie sous forme de kaïnite. Dans les sols argileux, il faut éviter de l'employer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95c682a4-6a5e-448b-ae03-0d32108ed890",
                        "source_entry_id": "70d39c8a-6ef1-37f6-ac15-cf814087449b",
                        "source_sense_description": "composed of clay or containing (much) clay",
                        "target_lang_word": "glaiseux",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "glaiseux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8afb44ac-7c9e-3105-9d65-532ae23eb4d9",
                                        "entry_id": "90fc6575-5b3e-32e8-b015-8cd3f20f7c8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est de la nature de la glaise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74be6228-4227-4313-8738-e577d61f6bfd",
                                                "sense_id": "8afb44ac-7c9e-3105-9d65-532ae23eb4d9",
                                                "text": "« — Que voulez-vous, les vents contraires ont soufflé jusqu’à avril ; en mai, le sol est devenu glaiseux ; en juin, il s’est craquelé ; au début de juillet apparurent les premières tornades."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5093255c-fc27-46a9-9eaf-50cac0ae0a33",
                                                "sense_id": "8afb44ac-7c9e-3105-9d65-532ae23eb4d9",
                                                "text": "Pater ne répond pas ; il se contente de jurer pour son compte sous les mols décombres où il s’empêtre et bientôt, avec des flocs sinistres, je le vois soulever lentement sur son dos rond la couverture, lourde comme un suaire glaiseux."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edaf82ac-7510-4625-b32d-b751832d615c",
                                                "sense_id": "8afb44ac-7c9e-3105-9d65-532ae23eb4d9",
                                                "text": "Mais la terre jaunâtre et glaiseuse du Perche, désignée dans le pays sous le nom de gruette ou de bournais, exige périodiquement des marnages, en raison de son acidité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bad17c0-cd87-4979-bde5-0a54195e51a3",
                                                "sense_id": "8afb44ac-7c9e-3105-9d65-532ae23eb4d9",
                                                "text": "Après le repas, Papa nous a conduits jusqu’à la forêt de Kigwena pour voir les babouins. Nous avons marché presque une heure sur un petit sentier glaiseux sans rien repérer, excepté quelques touracos verts. — (Gaël Faye, Petit Pays, Grasset, 2016, page 34)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "glaiseux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd679a88-2fe2-3690-a3d0-a5e5f612561c",
                                        "entry_id": "18b880ff-2146-3138-bae6-eb4a6abe0a5c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Paysan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cd64f5b-0f4e-425a-8620-0b822f35cf6c",
                                                "sense_id": "dd679a88-2fe2-3690-a3d0-a5e5f612561c",
                                                "text": "Le glaiseux et ses lardons"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19983e74-39da-4193-8543-e51d43e79f5c",
                                                "sense_id": "dd679a88-2fe2-3690-a3d0-a5e5f612561c",
                                                "text": "Si peu qu'il reste de terre héréditaire, si révoltés qu'en soient les hoirs, les seuls glaiseux peuvent dire ce que ça peut recoller aux pieds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7d0e4eb-94f7-482e-bf95-12f2cf2b8bd3",
                                                "sense_id": "dd679a88-2fe2-3690-a3d0-a5e5f612561c",
                                                "text": "Pitié! Je ne suis qu'un glaiseux!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
